// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : Doctor_Weber 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Doctor Weber 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P42661825" "Doctor Weber"
// ProfessionString :
"P1601631955" "Contract Arachnos Scientist"
// DescriptionString :
"P80065854" "Doctor Weber is known in the scientific community for ignoring ethics and morals to get what he needs. He has firsthand performed several atrocities in the name of scientific progress.<br><br>He has been shunned by most law abiding science groups, but has found temporary employment in Arachnos."
// LocationString :
// HelloString :
"P1714340980" "Let us give the people of Mercy a higher purpose, {HeroName}."
// IDontKnowYouString :
"P4218474871" "You and I have not met yet, {HeroName}. We have nothing to discuss until we can trust each other."
// NoTasksRemainingString :
"P481881440" "We're done together, for now, {HeroName}. I will be continuing work on my experiments with the Infected. Soon, I'm sure, we shall see the fruits of it."
// PlayerBusyString :
"P3276206449" "You have much on your mind, {HeroName}. Let us speak again when you have freed yourself from your current schemes."
// ComeBackLaterString :
"P856364347" ""
// FailsafeLevelString :
"P2472804946" "How is it that you can see my FailsafeLevelString?  That should be impossible, unless we've raised the level cap or you're peeking through .pigg files."
// IntroString :
"P2875613402" "Doctor Weber is one of our... 'contract' scientists. He is researching the Infected on Mercy Island, ever since our previous scientist was terminated.<br><br>He is unethical and amoral, the perfect person to do what needs to be done."
// IntroAcceptString :
"P3480180062" "Meet with Doctor Weber"
// IntroSendoffString :
"P3925931269" "You've made a wise choice with Doctor Weber. You two may even find that you have much in common, hrm?"
// IntroduceOneContact :
"P468004221" "Let me know when you wish to be introduced to one Lt. Harris."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page AgreedWeberTokenOwned Text :
"P4067079404" "Ah, {HeroName}, it is a pleasure to meet you again.<br><br>You've no doubt heard from Kuzmin that I am now studying the Infected. Unfortunately, Arachnos has... <i>insisted</i> that I allow their own full-time scientists to study the meteors.<br><br>That, I am fine with. The Infected are incredibly interesting. I believe you and I can find many <i>fascinating</i> aspects of them, with the help of the population of Mercy. Shall we begin?"
// Answer Text :
"P3611065572" "Yes, let's begin."
// Page DeclinedWeber Text :
"P3308880893" "Hrm, {HeroName}. I'm surprised to see you here. When last we spoke, you said you would not be meeting with me.<br><br>I suppose we all have our own change of heart.<br><br>Currently, as you've been told, I am studying the Infected here in Mercy. The fool, <color yellow>Dr. Geist</color>, who was studying this before me, went and got himself killed.<br><br>Unlucky for him, lucky for me. The Infected are proving to be fascinating creatures. I believe you and I can find some very interesting... <i>breakthroughs</i> with them. Shall we start?"
// Page NeverMetWeber Text :
"P1417028737" "Hello, {HeroName}. My name is <color yellow>Doctor Weber</color>. Operative Kuzmin has briefed me about your work against Longbow.<br><br>I believe you and I will get along just fine. I am currently investigating the Infected in Mercy Island. I've reached a point, however, where I could use the help of someone such as yourself.<br><br>I can tell you everything, once you're ready. Shall we?"
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


